      "problem": "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $Z∼N(0,1),$ compute $P(-2.25<Z<2.25).$\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.04\\,$ | $\\,0.05\\,$ | $\\,0.06\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,-2.3\\,$ | $\\,0.0096\\,$ | $\\,0.0094\\,$ | $\\,0.0091\\,$ |\n| $\\,-2.2\\,$ | $\\,0.0125\\,$ | $\\,0.0122\\,$ | $\\,0.0119\\,$ |\n| $\\,-2.1\\,$ | $\\,0.0162\\,$ | $\\,0.0158\\,$ | $\\,0.0154\\,$ |\n\n$P(-2.25<Z<2.25)=$\n{{field-1}}",
